**14. Migration Strategy**

**14.1 Tooling**

-   Migration tool: Flyway or Liquibase --- versioned, sequential SQL
    migration files

-   Every schema change is a new migration file --- never modify
    existing migrations

-   Migrations run automatically on deployment via CI/CD pipeline

-   All migrations are reversible --- every Up migration has a
    corresponding Down migration

**14.2 Migration File Naming Convention**

> V001\_\_create_tenants_table.sql
>
> V002\_\_create_users_table.sql
>
> V003\_\_create_projects_table.sql
>
> V004\_\_add_rls_policies.sql
>
> V005\_\_create_scheduling_tables.sql
>
> \...
>
> V040\_\_add_electrical_module_tables.sql
>
> V041\_\_add_plumbing_module_tables.sql

**14.3 RLS Policy Application**

RLS policies are applied in a dedicated migration after each table is
created. Policies must be re-applied after any table structural change.
The RLS migration pattern:

> \-- V004\_\_add_rls_policies.sql
>
> ALTER TABLE tenants ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
>
> ALTER TABLE users ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
>
> ALTER TABLE projects ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
>
> \-- \... all tenant-scoped tables
>
> CREATE POLICY tenant_isolation ON projects
>
> USING (tenant_id = current_setting(\'app.current_tenant_id\')::UUID)
>
> WITH CHECK (tenant_id =
> current_setting(\'app.current_tenant_id\')::UUID);

**14.4 updated_at Trigger**

A trigger automatically updates the updated_at column on every
modification:

> CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION set_updated_at()
>
> RETURNS TRIGGER AS \$\$
>
> BEGIN
>
> NEW.updated_at = NOW();
>
> RETURN NEW;
>
> END;
>
> \$\$ LANGUAGE plpgsql;
>
> \-- Apply to every table with updated_at
>
> CREATE TRIGGER trg_projects_updated_at
>
> BEFORE UPDATE ON projects
>
> FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION set_updated_at();

**11. Locale & Language Schema**

Locale preferences are stored at both the tenant level (company default)
and the user level (individual preference). User preference always takes
precedence. All string data is stored in its original language as
entered --- the platform does not translate stored content, only the UI
shell and system-generated text.

**11.1 Schema Additions for Localization**

  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Table**          **New Column**        **Type**      **Default**    **Description**
  ------------------ --------------------- ------------- -------------- --------------------------
  users              preferred_language    VARCHAR(10)   \'en\'         User\'s preferred UI
                                                                        language. ISO 639-1
                                                                        language code + optional
                                                                        region (e.g. \'es\',
                                                                        \'en\', \'pt-BR\',
                                                                        \'ht\'). Overrides tenant
                                                                        default. Set at signup via
                                                                        device locale detection,
                                                                        editable in Profile.

  tenants            default_language      VARCHAR(10)   \'en\'         Tenant-wide default
                                                                        language for new users and
                                                                        portal guests. Owner sets
                                                                        in Company Settings.
                                                                        Affects onboarding wizard
                                                                        language for new team
                                                                        members.

  user_invitations   preferred_language    VARCHAR(10)   NULL           Language to use for the
                                                                        invitation email. If NULL,
                                                                        uses
                                                                        tenant.default_language.
                                                                        Set by system based on
                                                                        context.

  notifications      locale                VARCHAR(10)   \'en\'         Locale used when the
                                                                        notification was generated
                                                                        --- stored so the
                                                                        notification record is
                                                                        self-descriptive even if
                                                                        user later changes
                                                                        language preference.

  daily_reports      language_detected     VARCHAR(10)   NULL           Detected language of the
                                                                        work_performed and issues
                                                                        text fields --- set by
                                                                        optional NLP pass for
                                                                        analytics. Non-blocking,
                                                                        best-effort.

  tenants            supported_languages   TEXT\[\]      \'{\"en\"}\'   Array of language codes
                                                                        the tenant has enabled for
                                                                        their workers. Defaults to
                                                                        \[\'en\'\]. When tenant
                                                                        enables Spanish,
                                                                        \[\'en\',\'es\'\] ---
                                                                        controls language selector
                                                                        options shown to users.
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

**11.2 Locale-Aware Field Behavior**

  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Field Type**     **Storage**            **Display**
  ------------------ ---------------------- ----------------------------------------
  Timestamps         Always stored as       Formatted for display using
                     TIMESTAMPTZ (UTC) ---  Intl.DateTimeFormat in user\'s locale on
                     locale-agnostic        the client

  Currency amounts   Always stored as       Formatted with Intl.NumberFormat(locale,
                     INTEGER (cents) ---    {style:\'currency\',currency:\'USD\'})
                     locale-agnostic        on client

  User-entered text  Stored as-is in        Displayed as stored --- platform does
  (notes,            whatever language the  not translate user content
  descriptions)      user typed --- no      
                     translation or         
                     normalization          

  System-generated   Stored as canonical    Translated on the client using i18n
  strings (status    English keys --- never keys: t(\'status.active\') → \'Active\'
  labels, type       locale-specific        or \'Activo\'
  values)            strings in the DB      

  Document names and Stored as uploaded --- Displayed as stored --- full Unicode
  filenames          supports Unicode fully support in all text fields
                     (UTF-8 throughout)     
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

**11.3 Migration Notes**

-   Add preferred_language and supported_languages to tenants migration:
    ALTER TABLE tenants ADD COLUMN default_language VARCHAR(10) NOT NULL
    DEFAULT \'en\', ADD COLUMN supported_languages TEXT\[\] NOT NULL
    DEFAULT \'{\"en\"}\'

-   Add preferred_language to users migration: ALTER TABLE users ADD
    COLUMN preferred_language VARCHAR(10) NOT NULL DEFAULT \'en\'

-   All existing tenant and user records default to \'en\' --- no data
    migration required

-   Index on users.preferred_language is NOT needed --- low cardinality,
    not used in WHERE clauses for filtering

-   Language codes follow IETF BCP 47 standard: \'en\', \'es\',
    \'pt-BR\', \'ht\', \'pl\', \'uk\', \'vi\', \'tl\', \'ar\', \'zh-CN\'
